I’m going to try the same overlap idea where it has a better chance: `dim=384` already has normalized `x`, so `out_gate = x @ Wog.T` can run on a side stream without recomputing layer norm. The main stream will compute only the first four projections needed for left/right, then BMM while the side stream computes `out_gate`.
